# Authorization headers, with the VS Code shorthands. user and password come
# from the env files.

### Basic, user:password shorthand
GET {{baseUrl}}/basic-auth/{{user}}/{{password}}
Authorization: Basic {{user}}:{{password}}

### Basic, user password shorthand
GET {{baseUrl}}/basic-auth/scott/tiger
Authorization: Basic scott tiger

### Basic with a wrong password, expect 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/basic-auth/scott/tiger
Authorization: Basic scott lion

### Digest shorthand
GET {{baseUrl}}/digest-auth/auth/scott/tiger
Authorization: Digest scott tiger

### Bearer token from the private env file
GET {{baseUrl}}/bearer/{{token}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### API key from .env
GET {{baseUrl}}/headers
X-Api-Key: {{$dotenv API_KEY}}
